  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1220 AM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nMoisture advection will be the rule from Saturday night through\nMonday as the Baja low fills and ejects northeast into the region,\nbringing Pacific moisture and increasing chances for precipitation.\nThis will be a top-down moistening process favoring western NM \nthrough Monday. All eyes turn to a potent upper level low diving \nsouth offshore of CA Tuesday, which is forecast to turn inland \nover SoCal on Wednesday. PWATs are forecast to rise further \nthrough Thursday as the upper level low fills and lifts northeast \nacross the region, steering remnant tropical moisture into NM. \nThursday still looks to be the wettest day next week and our \nforecast PoPs continue to trend up. This will be a warmer system, \nso rain is likely from the mid-slopes of the mountains into the \nlower elevations with snow across the peaks. The 00Z medium range \nmodel solutions are generally agreeable through at least Thursday,\nso forecast confidence is moderate to high for a return to wetter\nconditions next week.",
